        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-06-14T07:46:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't know if I'm not reading the card right, or it's a bug, but I took Guise for a test drive tonight (iOS, iPad), and encountered possible bugs with Uhh, Yeah I'm That Guy (UYITG):</p><p>(1) Playing with DW Fixer. &nbsp;Fixer had out Jack Handle and Alternating Tiger Claw. &nbsp;Guise&nbsp;<span>was first in turn order, before Fixer. &nbsp;Guise played</span>&nbsp;Lemme See That to take the Jack Handle, then used Hard Choices to play UYITG. &nbsp;I played UYITG, gave Fixer the \"high-five\" -- it then proceed to say \"UYTIG was destroyed!\", then do the requisite damage to all targets. &nbsp;Fixer's turn was next, and when he went to use Bitter Strike and it asked to destroy an ongoing, suddenly UYTIG was back in play, available to be destroyed.</p><p>(2) Legacy. &nbsp; A couple of turns later, Legacy had Inspiring Presence and Motivational Charge in play. &nbsp;Guise played Retcon to destroy an environment card, then used its power to draw UYITG. &nbsp;Guise then used Hard Choices to play UYITG. &nbsp;Instantly, Motivational Charge \"activated,\" healing everybody 1 HP, but it didn't \"activate\" for the 2 melee damage. Instead, Guise's damage from Hard Choices activated, doing 1 HP, +1 for Galvanize (which was still active), +1 for Inspiring Presence, and +1 from UYITG duplicating Inspiring Presence.</p><p>However:</p><p>(a) why did the \"power\" portion of &nbsp;Motivational Charge activate? &nbsp;If I'm reading UYITG correctly, it just says (paraphrasing) to act as if you had all of that hero's Ongoings. Motivational Charge doesn't do anything on its own; it requires using a power for it to work. &nbsp;Why did it \"activate\" -- is it because Guise played UYITG as part of his Power phase?</p><p>(b) If Motivational Charge's power activated, then shouldn't the whole thing have activated? &nbsp;I.e., not just the +1 healing for every hero, but the 2 melee damage as well? &nbsp; If playing UYITG during the power phase means that you activate any of the powers on the Ongoing cards you \"borrow,\" then shouldn't the order have gone:</p><p>1. &nbsp; &nbsp;Guise uses Hard Choices</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;A. &nbsp; &nbsp; Hard Choices, Part 1: &nbsp;Guise chooses to play card (UYITG), copies Legacy:</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(I) &nbsp; &nbsp; Motivational Charge under Legacy \"activates\"; all heroes heal +1 HP, and then Guise (as Legacy) does 2 melee damage (plus any buffs) to a target;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;B. &nbsp; &nbsp; Hard Choices, Part 2: &nbsp;Guise does 1 pt melee damage (plus any buffs)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
