        "raw": "<p>I don&#39;t know if I&#39;m not reading the card right, or it&#39;s a bug, but I took Guise for a test drive tonight (iOS, iPad), and encountered possible bugs with Uhh, Yeah I&#39;m That Guy (UYITG):</p><p>(1) Playing with DW Fixer. &nbsp;Fixer had out Jack Handle and Alternating Tiger Claw. &nbsp;Guise&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">was first in turn order, before Fixer. &nbsp;Guise played</span>&nbsp;Lemme See That to take the Jack Handle, then used Hard Choices to play UYITG. &nbsp;I played UYITG, gave Fixer the &quot;high-five&quot; -- it then proceed to say &quot;UYTIG was destroyed!&quot;, then do the requisite damage to all targets. &nbsp;Fixer&#39;s turn was next, and when he went to use Bitter Strike and it asked to destroy an ongoing, suddenly UYTIG was back in play, available to be destroyed.</p><p>(2) Legacy. &nbsp; A couple of turns later, Legacy had Inspiring Presence and Motivational Charge in play. &nbsp;Guise played Retcon to destroy an environment card, then used its power to draw UYITG. &nbsp;Guise then used Hard Choices to play UYITG. &nbsp;Instantly, Motivational Charge &quot;activated,&quot; healing everybody 1 HP, but it didn&#39;t &quot;activate&quot; for the 2 melee damage. Instead, Guise&#39;s damage from Hard Choices activated, doing 1 HP, +1 for Galvanize (which was still active), +1 for Inspiring Presence, and +1 from UYITG duplicating Inspiring Presence.</p><p>However:</p><p>(a) why did the &quot;power&quot; portion of &nbsp;Motivational Charge activate? &nbsp;If I&#39;m reading UYITG correctly, it just says (paraphrasing) to act as if you had all of that hero&#39;s Ongoings. Motivational Charge doesn&#39;t do anything on its own; it requires using a power for it to work. &nbsp;Why did it &quot;activate&quot; -- is it because Guise played UYITG as part of his Power phase?</p><p>(b) If Motivational Charge&#39;s power activated, then shouldn&#39;t the whole thing have activated? &nbsp;I.e., not just the +1 healing for every hero, but the 2 melee damage as well? &nbsp; If playing UYITG during the power phase means that you activate any of the powers on the Ongoing cards you &quot;borrow,&quot; then shouldn&#39;t the order have gone:</p><p>1. &nbsp; &nbsp;Guise uses Hard Choices</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;A. &nbsp; &nbsp; Hard Choices, Part 1: &nbsp;Guise chooses to play card (UYITG), copies Legacy:</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(I) &nbsp; &nbsp; Motivational Charge under Legacy &quot;activates&quot;; all heroes heal +1 HP, and then Guise (as Legacy) does 2 melee damage (plus any buffs) to a target;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;B. &nbsp; &nbsp; Hard Choices, Part 2: &nbsp;Guise does 1 pt melee damage (plus any buffs)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
